{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794050398,"nonce":"6SAjeiQdu5Iir5cKzL7h2gia3iU=","title":"Cache scope: one forge call per cached Run to read the default branch","message":"Creating an ungoverned Run with a ref and a `cache:` Step asks the forge for the default branch, which is the fallback read scope (efcec77, #100). That is one extra forge API call per such Run. If the forge does not answer, the Run reads only its own scope.\n\nOption: keep the default branch on the Project, updated from repository webhooks or a periodic sync.","files":null}]}